gxSp5uWfkZ6sRbY_R_vF7nlKLRk7uKu9wkJe3BVvVk=", "uri": "https://mediagateway.sweet.io/media/token/8bMLm51d/10724759562629414912/poster-image-square.png"}], "reverse_image": null}, "attributes": [{"name": "Audio Type", "value": "Sounds of the Game"}, {"name": "Crafted from Editions", "value": "344,487,477,376,359,333,265,250,499"}, {"name": "Crafted from Rarity", "value": "Limited"}, {"name": "Date", "value": "2008-10-24"}, {"name": "Edition Number", "value": "1"}, {"name": "Moment UUID", "value": "b572cf356a9d000094d6000000000000"}, {"name": "Play", "value": "Goal"}, {"name": "Player", "value": "Marian Hossa"}, {"name": "Rarity", "value": "Heroic"}, {"name": "Series", "value": "Series 3"}, {"name": "Series UUID", "value": "b572cf35000000000000000000000000"}, {"name": "Set", "value": "Signature Limiteds"}, {"name": "Set UUID", "value": "b572cf356a9d00000000000000000000"}, {"name": "Team", "value": "Detroit Red Wings"}], "creator": {"name": "SocialSweet Inc.", "uri": "https://sweet.io"}, "description": "Marian Hossa joined the Detroit Red Wings in July 2008, bringing his elite scoring ability to a team hungry for another Stanley Cup. On October 24, 2008, he put on a show against his former team, the Atlanta Thrashers, scoring two goals and adding an assist in a 5\u20133 win at Joe Louis Arena. His first goal was a thing of beauty\u2014he slipped past a defender, beat the goalie around the post, and tucked the puck in to give Detroit a 2\u20131 lead. Hossa finished the season with 40 goals and 31 assists in 74 games, playing a key role in the Red Wings\u2019 success. The next year, he signed with Chicago and went on to win three Stanley Cups.\r\n\r\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).", "edition_number": "1", "fees": [{"basis_points": 600, "recipient_address": "0x2B1